# Obsidian Vault: {{VAULT_NAME}}

Agents workspace for {{ECOSYSTEM_NAME}}. {{VAULT_PURPOSE}} This is the vault every session from every tool writes to. It holds machine state, queues, session notes, handoffs and skill evidence. Human-curated knowledge belongs in a personal or operations vault.

## Vault root

The root holds only `AGENTS.md`, `log.md`, the folders listed below and hidden tool-config folders (`.obsidian/`, `.claude/`). Anything else, including a loose `YYYY-MM-DD *.md` note, is a leaked write: file it or remove it. Every report a skill writes has a home in the table below, so do not invent a root folder for one.

{{TOP_LEVEL_FOLDERS_LIST}}

## Where things go

| Output | Path |
|--------|------|
| Session note | `Sessions/YYYY-MM-DD <slug>.md` |
| Handoff or pickup prompt | `Sessions/Handoffs/` |
| Audit, one-off review, retrospective | `Audits/<agent>/`; cross-agent synthesis at `Audits/` root |
| A skill's evidence: renders, probes, measurements, extraction records, the work-graph trio of a programme | `Ops/<skill-or-programme>/` |
| A skill's append-only journal | `Ops/<skill>-log.md` |
| A current-state report, overwritten on each run | `Ops/<report>.md`, with `generated_at` in frontmatter so its freshness shows the job that writes it is alive |
| Agent runtime state | `<Agent>/` |
| Workstation setup note (fleet) | `Workstations/Setup/` |

A work graph lives with the project it describes, never here: its `derive:` block resolves sources relative to the state file.

## Agent folders

{{AGENT_UNIVERSES}}

Agent folders are runtime data. Do not hand-edit unless triaging; the next tick may overwrite. Give every new output folder a row in the agent's table, with a retention window, before the job that writes it goes live. Do not re-create a folder that a table marks deleted.

## Sessions

Session notes file flat at `Sessions/` root, one note per session, `YYYY-MM-DD <slug>.md`, with the first eight characters of the session id appended when the name is taken that day. The `agent:` field discriminates the source (`claude-code`, `codex`, `cmux`, and whatever else you run); any dashboard over the folder groups on it. `Sessions/Handoffs/` holds pickup prompts and `Sessions/Archive/` older notes and retired working material.

Standard session frontmatter:

```yaml
---
categories:
  - "[[Sessions]]"
type: "[[Sessions]]"
agent: claude-code
model: <model id>
date: YYYY-MM-DD
status: in-progress
ended: YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM
workspace_name: "<name>"
workspace_id: "<uuid>"
goal: |
  <one-paragraph goal>
definition_of_done:
related:
  - "[[Sessions]]"
created: YYYY-MM-DD
---
```

### Session `status:` is a closed vocabulary

A dashboard groups on the literal string, so a value outside this set gets its own one-off heading and the note is effectively lost.

`queued` → `in-progress` → `review` → `done`, plus `blocked` (waiting on a human or an external event) and `failed` (ended without achieving its goal). Six values, nothing else.

- **Lowercase and hyphenated, never quoted.** `status: in-progress`. Quoting defeats tooling that matches on the bare value.
- **`done` means off the board.** When closing a session whose outcome was never recorded, say so in `## Outcome` rather than letting `done` imply the work shipped.
- **Do not normalise `failed` to `done`.** It carries information `done` destroys.

## Audits

Per-agent audits sit under `Audits/<agent>/`; cross-agent synthesis notes sit at `Audits/` root; a large historical sweep gets its own dated folder such as `Audits/YYYY-MM-DD restructure sweep/`. Audit files keep incident evidence, restructure notes and retrospectives indefinitely.

## Ops

Evidence and reports written by skills. Three kinds live here: append-only journals, one per skill family (`<family>-log.md`); current-state reports overwritten on each run; and artefact corpora a skill produces about its own build, each under `Ops/<name>/`. Operations and projects vaults hold their own subject matter, while a skill's engineering evidence lands here.

## Secrets

{{SECRETS_DIR_DESCRIPTION}}

Master credentials never sit inline anywhere in this vault. Agents read entries through a secrets-CLI helper, never by parsing markdown.

## Filing rules

- **YYYY-MM-DD dates everywhere** — filenames, frontmatter, directory names
- **Lowercase property keys**, plural for lists, snake_case for multi-word keys
- **No wikilinks to other vaults** — reference other-vault files by relative description, because paths change
- **Auto-generated index files** are never hand-edited. Edit the canonical source and rerun the generator.

## Property standards

| Property | Type | Usage |
|----------|------|-------|
| `agent` | text | which agent or host wrote this file |
| `status` | text | the closed session vocabulary above; free text on other note types |
| `created` | date | YYYY-MM-DD |
| `date` | date | the date the content relates to |
| `generated_at` | datetime | on a current-state report, the run that wrote it |
| `workspace_id` | text | cmux workspace UUID |
| `workspace_name` | text | cmux workspace name |

Only keys are constrained; values keep normal casing, except session `status:`.

## Retention

Agents vaults accumulate state and need periodic cleanup. Give every new output folder its own row.

| Path pattern | Retention |
|--------------|-----------|
| `Sessions/*.md` with `status: done` or `failed` | 30 days → `Sessions/Archive/` |
| `Audits/**` | indefinite |
| `Ops/<skill>-log.md` | indefinite |
| `Ops/<report>.md` | superseded in place |
| `Ops/<name>/` corpora | until the work they describe is retired |
| `<Agent>/**` | per the agent's own table |

## Boundary rule

Agents write freely to their own folders in this vault. Writes to **other** vaults need explicit cross-vault approval through the H0 primitive; agents never write across a vault boundary directly.

## Maintenance entrypoints

| Command | Behaviour on this vault |
|---------|-------------------------|
| Sweep | The full pipeline: reconcile sessions, audit filing, apply retention |
| Organise | Filing audit against the vault-root rule and the where-things-go table |
| Reconcile | Close session notes whose workspace is gone, and check agent health |

## Vault log

`log.md` is the append-only operational log for structural changes to this vault. Agents log their own runs to their own `<Agent>/ops/` or `<Agent>/sessions/` folders.

