## Kepano knowledge rules (agents-vault pointer)

If you keep one canonical copy of these rules elsewhere and sync it into each vault, the sentinel comments mark the managed region and edits inside the pair are overwritten on the next sync. Otherwise treat this block as yours to edit.

Agents vaults are runtime substrate: session logs, ops state and queues. Their local standards cover the property and retention rules needed in this vault.

- **Rules that apply when writing notes in this vault** — YAML property naming (lowercase snake_case keys), `YYYY-MM-DD` dates everywhere, plural keys for lists / singular for single values — are stated in this vault's own **Property Standards** section above. That section is the operative reference.
- **The full universal canon** — categories against folders, wikilink conventions, the standard-property and deprecated-property tables, the rating scale, HTML in notes — is carried in the personal and operations vault templates in this skill. An operational vault does not need it loaded every session, so read it there on demand.

